Agent 1: **Step 1: Determine the total distance that must be cleared.**  
Each train is 260 m long, so when they cross completely the front of one train must travel the length of both trains.  
\[
\text{Total distance}=260\text{ m}+260\text{ m}=520\text{ m}
\]

**Step 2: Convert the individual speeds to metres per second.**  

\[
\begin{aligned}
80\ \text{km/h} &= 80 \times \frac{1000}{3600}\ \text{m/s}= \frac{200}{9}\ \text{m/s}\approx 22.22\ \text{m/s}\\[4pt]
70\ \text{km/h} &= 70 \times \frac{1000}{3600}\ \text{m/s}= \frac{175}{9}\ \text{m/s}\approx 19.44\ \text{m/s}
\end{aligned}
\]

**Step 3: Compute the relative speed (since they move toward each other).**  

\[
v_{\text{rel}} = \frac{200}{9} + \frac{175}{9}= \frac{375}{9}= \frac{125}{3}\ \text{m/s}\approx 41.67\ \text{m/s}
\]

**Step 4: Calculate the time required to cover the total distance at the relative speed.**  

\[
\text{Time}= \frac{\text{Total distance}}{v_{\text{rel}}}= \frac{520\ \text{m}}{125/3\ \text{m/s}} = 520 \times \frac{3}{125}= \frac{1560}{125}=12.48\ \text{s}
\]

